**Stratified vs. headline.** Applying the stratified CFR row-by-row gives **~830 deaths/year**; applying the flat headline 12.5 % gives **~1,460 deaths/year**; the Stats SA Vital Registration triangulation gives **~960–2,000 deaths/year**. The headline range **1,500–1,800** sits in the upper-mid VR range and is what all three policy briefs cite. The full v2 → v3 rationale is in [`parameter_appraisal.qmd`](parameter_appraisal.qmd).

